  "$material": "gsm is the real cloth weight, grams per square metre. fluidity 0..1 is how far it abandons the cut and falls to the body: 0 holds the shape it was cut to, 1 pours straight down. crease 0..1 is how well it KEEPS a fold once made \u2014 linen is near the top, wool near the bottom because its creases hang out. These three describe the cloth; bend/density/damping are how the solver is made to behave like it. thickness is the real cloth thickness in MILLIMETRES. At a figure's scale it is far too small to draw literally \u2014 2.6mm on a 160cm woman is a sixth of a percent \u2014 so it shows the way it shows on a real garment: thick cloth cannot turn a tight corner, so its hem corners round off, and its cut edges read heavier.",
